The mount table on WitOS (plan step C1.2), as in the release/10.0 set: the TARGET_WITOS branch opens /etc/mtab,
which the system layer's libc serves in mntent form from the namespace's mount points, where Linux opens
/proc/mounts; the parsing is upstream's. The 8.0 file differs from 10.0's above this hunk (getmntinfo rather than
getfsstat), so the hunk's offset differs and its bytes are the same.

